    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-efficiency matchup of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who leads our starters with a 74.56 score. His clash against Bieber (R) is optimized by a 5.25 xERA and a potent 14% platoon edge, making him our premier play. **Drake Baldwin** also provides elite production at 68.29; his slotting in the leadoff spot combined with a favorable 4.60 xERA matchup against Pfaadt gives him the highest ceiling in our active group. Furthermore, **Jacob Wilson** benefits significantly from a 10% park factor lift, cementing his status as a core start despite the respectable 4.21 xERA of Rocker (R).\n\nWhile our starting nine remains aggressive, the benching of **Jackson Merrill** was the most difficult pivot. With a score of 50.88, **Jackson Merrill** narrowly missed the cut, primarily due to the 2.90 xERA of Williams (G), which significantly dampened his projected output relative to the other high-upside plays. We are also monitoring the risk associated with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**; while both are active, they face Matz (L), forcing us to lean into their dynamic platoon splits and the aggressive base-running environment provided by the pitcher's slow delivery. We are notably cautious with **Nasim Nunez**, who faces a defensive tax due to an elite opposing catcher, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, whose raw power is slightly countered by the high-hold efficiency of the opposing battery. We will keep **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Luis Lara** on standby, though their sub-50 projections confirm that our current active configuration is the optimal path for maximizing our 5x5 categories.",
